        "notes": "Reviewed all four steps, the two exact dependencies and Bianchi §§1.2,1.4. Both chord/epigraph directions handle infinite values and t=0,1 with the explicit 0·infinity convention. Step 1.3 gives a direct Euclidean-ball proof for weak sublevels; step 2.1 uses an intermediate finite height even when f(x)=infinity and an explicit product neighborhood. Empty sublevels, empty epigraph and identically infinite f are permitted; properness is not needed. No AC. Current expanded step 1.3 is sound but differs from the abbreviated contract derivation, which is synchronized to the current carrier below."
