          "claim": "Equality means every $y\\in\\operatorname{dom}f$ satisfies $\\langle p,y\\rangle-f(y)\\le\\langle p,x\\rangle-f(x)$, which rearranges to the subgradient inequality; for $y\\notin\\operatorname{dom}f$ that inequality is automatic because $f(y)=+\\infty$. Conversely the subgradient inequalities make the value at $x$ a finite upper bound attained there, so $f^*(p)=\\langle p,x\\rangle-f(x)$.",
          "step": "2.1",
