      "risk_review": {
        "status": "complete",
        "reviewer": "alpha-batch-4",
        "notes": "Reviewed six steps and all twelve exact suppliers. Positive integers m,d make the simplex and Euclidean compactness legal. Nonempty fibers on P are compact and the linear objective attains a finite minimum. The compact image C plus upward ray has exactly the minimized epigraph; the explicit continuous distance-to-ray formula has positive compact minimum off C+V, proving closedness without subsequence choice. Convexity is direct; the finite-weight induction includes N=1 and divides only by 1−theta_j>0. Greatest-minorant inequality is automatic outside P. Biconjugation requires precisely the established closed proper convex hypotheses. Fenchel equality and zero weighted slack force equality only on occupied data points. Repeated points, zero weights, one datum and boundary fibers are covered. No AC, infinite-family claim or physical conclusion."
      }
