      "risk_review": {
        "status": "complete",
        "reviewer": "alpha-batch-4",
        "notes": "Reviewed both steps and all five direct suppliers, including the current draft batch-3 point-mass, mass, comparison, additive-representation carriers and the signed/cancellation/reference-supremum proof chain. Finite coefficients S(s_i) are supplied by the explicitly assumed strict-reference representation. Unit point masses have mass one; zero coefficients are omitted rather than used in a positive-scaling axiom. Distinct states make theta -> M_theta injective even with coincident q_i, so each coordinate fiber is exactly Theta_x. The affine chi hypothesis and explicit a_i:=S(s_i) instantiate the finite-mixture theorem in positive dimensions, with its empty-fiber convention. Normalization, attainment, lsc, convexity, biconjugation and occupied-point support all inherit that same finite data. No empirical conclusion or independent acceptance of the draft representation is claimed. One-state, zero-weight, coincident-coordinate and empty-coordinate-fiber cases are covered; no AC. The refuter correctly identified the former unbound a_i, a nonfatal specification defect now repaired."
      }
