      "risk_review": {
        "status": "complete",
        "reviewer": "alpha-batch-4",
        "notes": "Checked steps 1.1–3.1 and all nine cited suppliers: the pointwise directional identity at every x gives twice differentiable line restrictions, so MVT for phi and phi prime is legitimate. Positive curvature has a uniform positive minimum on the nonempty compact sphere in ker A; finite entry continuity gives a uniform neighborhood bound. Negative curvature gives arbitrarily close lower feasible values. The ker A={0} branch avoids an empty sphere and is vacuously a strict minimum; k=0 is permitted by the bounded-linear-map statement, while d≥1 matches Heine–Borel. Reader dimension clarification accepted; no proof change or AC. Cornell Bindel §6.1.3–6.1.4 provides context, while local proof supplies the precise affine test."
      }
