      "risk_review": {
        "status": "complete",
        "reviewer": "alpha-batch-4",
        "notes": "Checked all five steps and six cited exact suppliers. Active rows give nonnegative limiting changes by matrix continuity; inactive positive amounts permit a common positive finite minimum step bound, including the case of no restrictions. Constant h and t_k=epsilon/(k+1) witness the reverse inclusion without AC. Every tangent has a feasible ray, so differentiation gives necessity at a relative local minimum; convexity gives global sufficiency through the correctly directed secant inequality. Chain rule on the open amount domain yields nu transpose mu; zero h, empty active set and rank-deficient nu are covered. Cornell Bindel §6.1.4 is context; the local proof supplies the exact polyhedral formula. No empirical premise."
