        }
      ],
      "risk_review": {
        "status": "complete",
        "reviewer": "alpha-batch-4",
        "notes": "Checked steps 1.1–3.1 and all seven cited supplier statements/definitions. The chosen column permutation is a linear homeomorphism with constant derivative; the chosen minor becomes the invertible v block. q<n ensures both IFT dimensions are positive, and the supplier allows shrinking to keep that block invertible along the graph. The graph/projection maps give precisely the locally defined graph dimension, not a global phase count. q=n uses the separate inverse-function result and injectivity, avoiding a nonexistent R^0 IFT. The stipulated minor is an input, so no rank theorem or choice gap."
      }
