          "case_scope": {
            "source_section": "Example",
            "source_excerpt": "Let $f:\\mathbb R\\to\\{0,+\\infty\\}$ be the indicator of $[0,\\infty)$: $f(y)=0$ for $y\\ge0$ and $f(y)=+\\infty$ for $y<0$. At $z=(-1,0)$, the epigraph is separated by a vertical hyperplane (one whose coefficient of the epigraph-height coordinate is zero). The conjugate is $f^*(p)=0$ for $p\\le0$ and $+\\infty$ for $p>0$, so $f^{**}(-1)=+\\infty=f(-1)$. The affine minorants $\\ell_k(y)=-ky$, $k\\ge0$, display the unbounded dual values at $y=-1$.",
