          "reason": "The zero tilt $f(y)-0\\cdot y$ has every point of the interval as a minimizer, and $f^*(0)=0$ is attained at every such point. Boundary iff-forward: The example makes no biconditional assertion.",
          "case_scope": {
            "source_section": "Example",
            "source_excerpt": "Let $f$ be the indicator of $[-1,1]$. The zero tilt $f(y)-0\\cdot y$ has every point of the interval as a minimizer, and $f^*(0)=0$ is attained at every such point. Equivalently, $0\\in\\partial f(x)$ for every $x\\in[-1,1]$. Thus the supporting face at slope zero is the whole interval, and coercive Fenchel attainment need not be unique.",
            "current_raw_sha256": "3d1f152062d640f480c7404d3c7c504de90719763a72fb144f0aa68d9820179e",
