            "source_excerpt": "For the reaction $2\\,\\mathrm{H_2}+\\mathrm{O_2}\\to2\\,\\mathrm{H_2O}$, let extent $\\xi$ and species amounts use moles. The dimensionless stoichiometric column is $\\nu=(-2,-1,2)^{\\mathsf T}$ in the species order $(\\mathrm{H_2},\\mathrm{O_2},\\mathrm{H_2O})$, and take $n^0=(2,1,0)^{\\mathsf T}$. Then the feasible extent interval is $[0,1]$, and at $\\xi=0$ the tangent cone permits only forward directions $h\\ge0$. The matrix of hydrogen and oxygen atom counts annihilates $\\nu$. For the explicitly mathematical objective $\\Phi(n)=n_{\\mathrm{H_2O}}$, the induced extent function is $f(\\xi)=2\\xi$ and has a boundary minimum at zero. This is a stoichiometric calculation, not a claim about chemical equilibrium or a measured system.",
