        "notes": "Checked steps 1.1–3.1 and all six exact cited supplier statements/definitions. One-sided differentiation of the stated segment inequality gives the supporting bound; affine stationarity kills y−x*, and the midpoint argument gives uniqueness only with strict concavity and convex F. The line restriction is C² by the cited derivative and chain rules; MVT on R gives the o(t²) remainder also for negative t. Zero h and coincident endpoints are harmless. The local midpoint condition yields only nonpositive curvature, with no strictness or global convexity inferred. Bianchi §1.5 is context; the argument is complete locally. No AC or physics premise."
